Wait - parseDuration on buf is synchronous; ffprobe is async and needs the file on disk. So write file first, then probe, then fallback to parseDuration(buf). Order: write file → probe (async) → if null, parseDuration. Good.

Note about stored_filename: we insert with stored_filename = '' then update. The column is NOT NULL so empty string is fine. Actually let me just compute stored filename BEFORE insert using a random UUID instead: stored = `${randomUUID()}.${ext}`. Then insert in one statement with the real filename. This is cleaner and avoids the double update. But spec wants `uploads/<group-id>/<track-id>.mp3`. Using track id in the name is nicer for debugging. I'll do the insert-then-update approach to keep the id-based filename. Both fine.

Actually, simpler: keep track id-based naming but do:
