Tailwind CSS v4 error: "Cannot apply unknown utility class `btn`". The issue: in Tailwind v4, `@apply` inside `@layer components` referencing a custom class like `.btn-primary { @apply btn ... }` fails because `btn` is a component class, not a utility. In v4, to apply custom classes you need `@reference` or to define them properly. Actually the error is specifically "Cannot apply unknown utility class `btn`" — because `btn` is a custom class defined in the same stylesheet, and `@apply btn` doesn't work for custom classes in v4.

In Tailwind v4, `@apply` can only use utilities (and things registered via `@utility`). To reference custom classes, use `@utility` or `@reference`, or use the `@apply` with a defined custom utility.

The simplest fix: don't use `@apply btn` inside `.btn-primary`. Instead, write the full set of properties or restructure. Options:

1. Use CSS custom properties: define `.btn { @apply ...; }` and then `.btn-primary { @apply inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-full px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold transition focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-fuchsia-400 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50 bg-gradient-to-r from-violet-600 to-fuchsia-600 text-white shadow-lg shadow-fuchsia-900/30 hover:from-violet-500 hover:to-fuchsia-500 active:scale-[0.98]; }` — i.e., duplicate the base properties. Ugly but works.

